# Q1
c("Q1.1",AP,"OBSERVED_FACT","KNOWN",AU,S,"National apparel purchase intent in July 2026 was 37.6%: the share of U.S. adults who said they plan to buy apparel in the next 30 days.","national_monthly 2026-07 intent_pct 37.6; methodology_summary definition ("+MS+"); M1","Figure and definition read directly from licensed sources.")
c("Q1.2",AP,"OBSERVED_FACT","KNOWN",AU,S,"It is based on 3,053 respondents and has a 95% margin of error of plus or minus 2.0 points,","national_monthly 2026-07 n 3053, moe95_pts 2.0; M1","Read directly.")
c("Q1.3",AM,"DERIVED_FIGURE","KNOWN",AU,S,"which puts the 95% range at roughly 35.6% to 39.6%.","M1: 37.6 ± 2.0","Arithmetic correct; 'the true value is likely' replaced by a range statement (Challenger Q1.3 sustained).")
c("Q1.4",AP,"OBSERVED_FACT","KNOWN",AU,S,"That margin already allows for the effect of weighting the sample to Census benchmarks.","methodology_summary: margins 'include a design effect for weighting'","Directly supported.")
c("Q1.5",AM,"INFERENCE","INFERRED",AU,S,"As a rule of thumb, a change of less than about 3 points between two months at the national level is within sampling error.","M1: MOE of a two-month difference = sqrt(2.0^2+2.0^2) = 2.83, assuming independent monthly samples; national MOE 1.9-2.0 throughout","A's '2-3 points' understates the difference margin; independence is an assumption, hence INFERRED.")
c("Q1.6",AM,"INFERENCE","INFERRED",AU,S,"For example, the dip from June (38.3%) to July (37.6%) is not statistically distinguishable from no change.","M1: -0.7 vs 2.83","Stated as a statistical judgment rather than 'not meaningful'.")
