c("Q7.4",RJ,"INFERENCE","CONFLICTED",AU,CF,"The timing doesn't settle the question either way.","M3: South Feb->Mar rise recurs (+4.6 2024, +4.0 2025, +6.3 2026); South YoY gain +1.9/+2.6 Jan-Feb, +4.9 Mar, +5.4 Apr, +5.0 May, +11.9 Jun, +5.1 Jul, +7.7 Aug, each ±4.4-4.6","A's 'timing doesn't line up; the South had already jumped in March, before the window' argued one side. The unadjusted March jump is largely seasonal (against A), while the year-over-year series does step up around March (partly for A). Evidence points both ways: CONFLICTED, not CONTRADICTED (Challenger A2 sustained over the Analyst). The client is told only that timing does not settle it.")
c("Q7.5",AM,"OBSERVED_FACT","KNOWN",AU,S,"In 2026, South intent rose from 34.5% in February to 40.8% in March.","regional_monthly South 2026-02, 2026-03","The figures are true; they are kept only inside the seasonal context below, not as evidence against the openings.")
c("Q7.B1",AM,"INFERENCE","INFERRED",AU,S,"But South intent rises from February to March every year in our data (+4.6 points in 2024, +4.0 in 2025, +6.3 in 2026), so much of that jump is the usual seasonal pattern.","M3","Analyst addition; wording tempered from 'mostly' to 'much of' (6.3 vs prior 4.0-4.6).")
c("Q7.B2",AM,"INFERENCE","INFERRED",AU,S,"Compared with the same month a year earlier, the South's gain was about +2 to +3 points in January and February 2026, about +5 points in March, April, May and July, +11.9 in June and +7.7 in August. Each of these monthly comparisons has a margin of error of roughly ±4.5 points, so our data can't pin down when the change started, and national intent's year-over-year gain also grew over the same months. None of this measures what the openings contributed.","M3: South YoY by month; difference MOE 4.38-4.60; national YoY avg +1.9 Jan-Mar vs +3.36 Apr-Aug","Analyst's Jan-Mar/Apr-Aug split favoured the openings (March in the 'before' bin; June outlier). Monthly values stated without a split; no dating of the change and no South-minus-national 'excess' figure (which would read as an attribution and involves national, which includes the unlicensed West).")
c("Q7.6",AM,"OBSERVED_FACT","KNOWN",AU,S,"Other things also happened over the period: gasoline prices rose for a third straight month in March 2026, back-to-school promotions started earlier than usual at several national retailers in July, and consumer-confidence proxies ticked up in August. Our data can't separate their effects from the openings' either.","market_events entries 2026-03, 2026-07, 2026-08","A's 'all affect intent' was an unsupported causal claim (NOT_ESTABLISHED); Analyst's 'started early in July' misquoted the digest (Challenger A6). Events stated as coinciding, in the digest's words.")
c("Q7.8",AP,"INFERENCE","INFERRED",AU,S,"The survey measures intent. It isn't designed to separate the effect of any single event, and any points figure we gave you would be a guess.","methodology_summary (monthly intent survey; no attribution design)","Reasoned from the methodology.")
c("Q7.9",AM,"INFERENCE","INFERRED",AU,S,"Estimating the openings' effect would need a design built for that question, such as comparing markets near new stores with similar markets that got none. You could raise that with Halvorsen.","General method; account-team offer not established","Method advice is general and labeled as such; referral neutralized.")
